-- allocation-stress.once: Placeholder for allocation test patterns
--
-- NOTE: This test cannot yet be compiled because the current Malonzo-generated
-- compiler does not implement the 'pair' combinator. This file documents the
-- allocation patterns we intend to test once pair allocation is implemented.
--
-- Intended test patterns (for future implementation):
-- 1. Pairs immediately consumed (stack candidates)
--    - test_consume_fst: fst . diagonal
--    - test_consume_snd: snd . diagonal
-- 2. Pairs that escape by being returned (heap required)
--    - test_return_pair: diagonal (returns the pair)
--    - test_swap: pair snd fst (creates new pair that escapes)
-- 3. Nested pairs (mixed allocation)
--    - test_nested: pair diagonal id (outer escapes, inner consumed)
--
-- For now, we use a minimal identity function as a placeholder
-- that will allow the test infrastructure to compile.

